      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey can u explain exactly what the seller is responsible for under CIF incoterms 2020? i'm looking at a contract for some electronics shipping from korea to germany and just want to be sure about the transfer of risk vs cost.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Under the CIF (Cost, Insurance, and Freight) Incoterms 2020, the seller is responsible for the cost, insurance, and freight of the goods to the port of destination, which in your case is Germany. However, the risk of loss or damage to the goods, as well as any additional costs, such as unloading and import duties, transfers from the seller to the buyer once the goods are loaded onto the shipping vessel at the port of shipment in Korea. So, while the seller is taking care of the shipping and insurance, the buyer is responsible for the goods from that point forward. It's like a deal where the seller is the one who packs the goods and puts them on the ship, but once the ship leaves the port, the buyer is the one who has to worry about the goods. Just remember, in the world of shipping, it's always the buyer who has to watch out for the pesky goblins that might try to cause trouble once the goods are on the high seas.",
